 "guard_pairs_rows": {
  "decomposition": {
   "defined": true,
   "definition": "Both predictives are Student-t with the cell's degrees of freedom nu (P2 is moment matched in P1's family), so a row's log score is f(location, scale) = log of the density of theta + Normal(0, s_star^2) at y with theta ~ t(location, scale, nu). The difference f(loc2, sc2) - f(loc1, sc1) is split into a location part, the average of f(loc2, sc1) - f(loc1, sc1) and f(loc2, sc2) - f(loc1, sc2), and a scale part, the average of f(loc1, sc2) - f(loc1, sc1) and f(loc2, sc2) - f(loc2, sc1) (the two orders of changing one parameter at a time, averaged: the Shapley split of two players); the parts sum to the difference row by row. The locations and scales are those of the backtest's own predictives, refit at each admitted origin with the harness's factories and checked by recomputing both stored log scores.",
   "max_abs_recomputation_error": 0.0,
   "same_degrees_of_freedom": true
  },
